    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d835">

                <pb facs="0981" n="863" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg863"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.6212 A/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-12T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 12,
                                1928—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>23. Department handed German Ambassador March 12 a draft of a proposed treaty of
                    arbitration between the United States and Germany. The provisions of the draft
                    are identical in effect with those of the arbitration treaty recently signed
                    with France<anchor n="3" xml:id="d835-f1"/> and with draft arbitration treaties
                    already submitted to the Spanish,. British, Japanese, Italian and Norwegian
                        Governments.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d835-f2"/></p>
                <p>Department also handed to the Ambassador draft of treaty of similar purport to
                    the so-called Bryan Treaties.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d835-f3"/></p>
                <p>The text of these proposed treaties will be forwarded in next pouch.<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d835-f4"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d835-f1" n="3" xml:id="d835-f1-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg816">p. 816</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d835-f2" n="4" xml:id="d835-f2-content">
                <p>For negotiations with Great Britain, see <hi rendition="#italic">Post</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg945">pp. 945</ref> ff; with Italy, Japan, and Spain, see <ref
                        target="frus1928v03#pg_102">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, pp.
                        102</ref> ff., <ref target="frus1928v03#pg_135">pp. 135</ref> ff., and <ref
                        target="frus1928v03#pg_879">pp. 879</ref> ff. Although negotiations with
                    Norway were instituted in 1928, the treaty was not signed until 1929 (Department
                    of State Treaty Series No. 788).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d835-f3" n="5" xml:id="d835-f3-content">
                <p>For index references to the Bryan treaties, see <ref target="frus1914#pg_1130"
                            ><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1914, p. 1130</ref>;
                        <ref target="frus1915#pg_1328">1915, p. 1328</ref>; <ref
                        target="frus1916#pg_1007">1916, p. 1007</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d835-f4" n="6" xml:id="d835-f4-content">
                <p>Draft treaties not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
